{"user": "what's a good rule of thumb for these endgames so i dont get crushed like that again?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T20:54:58.914136+00:00", "assistant": "Good endgame rule of thumb: **don\u2019t maximize flips; maximize final stable discs.**\n\nBefore each move, ask:\n\n1. **Does this give away a corner?**  \n   Avoid playing next to an empty corner unless you\u2019ve calculated it.\n\n2. **Can I take/secure a corner or stable edge?**  \n   Corners can\u2019t be flipped, and edges attached to corners often become permanent.\n\n3. **What moves will White have after my move?**  \n   A \u201cquiet\u201d move that leaves White only bad moves is often better than a big flip.\n\n4. **Who moves last in each empty region?**  \n   In endgames, parity matters: often you want White to be forced to open the last dangerous square.\n\n5. **Count the finish, not the current flip.**  \n   If there are only a few empties, try to mentally play out both lines and compare final disc count.\n\nIn your game, the big lesson is: **White\u2019s corners/edges became stable, so your discs in the middle didn\u2019t matter enough.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T20:54:58.914136+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T20:55:03.914136+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0,